# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dataset - never committed. On Kaggle it is attached as an input; locally it is
# downloaded from Kaggle ("Chest CT-Scan images" by Mohamed Hany).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data/
data/
lung_colon_image_set
*.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trained weights (v2 LESSON 10, still in force)
# Ignored until `git lfs install` has been run and LFS tracking is confirmed
# working (`git lfs track` should list *.keras). After that, delete the two
# lines below to start committing weights through LFS.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
models/
*.keras
*.h5
*.hdf5

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated artefacts. The three results CSVs and the reports ARE tracked
# (see the negations below) because they are the deliverable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
outputs/figures/*
outputs/history/*
outputs/splits/*
!outputs/figures/.gitkeep
!outputs/history/.gitkeep
!outputs/reports/.gitkeep
!outputs/splits/.gitkeep

# outputs/predictions/ is deliberately NOT ignored (LESSON 5). One small CSV per
# run (a few hundred rows) is what lets a collapse check invented later be
# applied to an old run without retraining it - that is evidence, not clutter,
# and on a CPU-only project a retrain is not an affordable substitute.

# archive/ holds the frozen v1/v2 attempt and IS tracked - the lessons in the
# v3 README point at its evidence. Never regenerate or edit it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python / Jupyter / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local WSL virtual environment
.venv-wsl/

# Shared libraries / binary files
*.so
*.so*

# Phase 2 - local-only trained checkpoints (fair re-benchmark + the single
# MiniConvNet checkpoint run). These are large binary files that must never
# go through git; back them up manually (Drive, external disk, etc.) after
# running the notebook that produces them.
checkpoints_local/

# Phase 2 fair-benchmark predictions/histories/confusion matrices/figures are
# regenerable from checkpoints_local/ + the dataset, so they stay local too.
# The metrics CSV/JSON are small and ARE worth tracking - only the bulky,
# regenerable per-run artefacts are ignored here.
results/fair_baseline/predictions/
results/fair_baseline/histories/
results/fair_baseline/confusion_matrices/
results/fair_baseline/figures/
